AWS Cloud Engineer interview questions 

🔹 EKS pods can’t scale due to IP shortage
This usually happens when the VPC subnet CIDR is too small. The fix? Either add a secondary CIDR block or use the VPC CNI’s custom networking to expand the IP pool.
🔹 EC2 stuck in “pending” state
Often tied to the AMI or instance type. The AMI might not exist anymore or the chosen AZ doesn’t support that instance type. Always verify before launch.
🔹 ALB not balancing traffic evenly
If targets are healthy but distribution is uneven, check if sticky sessions are enabled or if cross-zone load balancing is turned off. Both can cause imbalance.
🔹 App can’t fetch secrets from Secrets Manager
Most likely an IAM permission issue (secretsmanager:GetSecretValue) or the wrong secret ARN in the code.
🔹 SQS queue messages piling up, Lambda not consuming
Check whether the event source mapping is configured between the Lambda and SQS, and confirm the Lambda’s IAM role has permission to read from the queue.
🔹 DynamoDB “ThrottlingException” during peak traffic
Enable auto-scaling for RCU/WCU or move to on-demand capacity. This way DynamoDB handles burst traffic gracefully.
🔹 EKS pods crashing with OOM (out-of-memory) errors
Look at the pod spec – resource requests/limits might be too low. Adjust them to align with the workload’s actual needs.
🔹 IAM user bypassing MFA
Enabling MFA alone isn’t enough. You need to enforce it via IAM policies that deny login if MFA isn’t present.
